# Cloud Build source-upload filter.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: without it gcloud falls back to .gitignore, which left docs/ (61MB of PNGs) +
# tools/ (38MB) in the tarball — ~99MB of the 100MB upload, none of it used by the Dockerfile (it only
# COPYs pyproject.toml, src/, main.py, worker.py, redis_worker.py). That upload timed out
# (`gcloud crashed (ReadTimeout)` to storage.googleapis.com) and killed a deploy before the build began.
#
# CAREFUL: this file REPLACES the .gitignore fallback, so every secret/junk exclusion is repeated here
# explicitly — dropping one would start uploading it.

# --- secrets / local config (were covered by .gitignore; MUST stay excluded) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.compose.example
*.tfvars
*.pem
*credentials*

# --- local env + caches ---
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.db
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.git/
.gitignore

# --- not used by the image build (the bulk of the old upload) ---
docs/
tools/
tests/
spikes/
*.md
!README.md
